Finger of death is a decent comparison.  I was just trying to restrict
it so it wasn't too powerful; any or many of those restrictions could
be relaxed. The key would be to actually code it (maybe as a clone of
finger of death, or an actual grant to the monk class of that spell)
and see how it works.

Within each of my patches, I try to keep things balanced and add some
depth with what already exists in the game, since it's very easy to
just toss in something to just make the game easier or harder.

My spell components (essences) patch definitely makes it harder, but I
think it draws you more into the world by creating a relationship
between what you kill and what you can cast.  The great thing about
this game is that it turns out to be really straightforward to map
spells to creature's in-game attributes.

